.env
.env.local
# Where a sweep is told which worker to reach. Machine-specific by nature —
# hostnames, tunnel ports, the name of the variable holding a key. The shape is
# committed as tools/bundle/worker.example.json.
tools/bundle/worker.local.json
*.log
# ...except under records/evidence/, where a log is not build output but the
# artefact a record cites. The D7 header's `cost.source` points at
# `d7-campaign.log`, and `tests/test_run_headers.py` asserts the path exists —
# which passed only on the machine that ran the campaign and was red in CI from
# the day it landed (#330, 2026-08-21; caught 2026-08-22). ADR-0026 lens 1:
# record the unrecoverable. A campaign log that lives on one laptop is exactly
# that, and a cited path nobody else can open is a citation in name only.
!records/evidence/**/*.log
# ...and one exception back the other way. `d7-campaign.aborted-run.log` is 282
# bytes whose whole content is reproduced verbatim in
# `d7-sleep.aborted-run.README.md`, which IS tracked, and two records state it
# is untracked (that README's own `## The driver log, verbatim`, and the
# 2026-08-19 session record). Nothing about it is unrecoverable, so tracking it
# would duplicate a record rather than preserve one — and would make two
# committed records wrong. Kept ignored, deliberately, so the exemption above
# reads as "a cited log is evidence" and not "every log is".
records/evidence/calibration-2026-08-19/d7-campaign.aborted-run.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
tools/breadth/worker.local.json
node_modules/
# The campaign driver's stop sentinel (tools/bench/serving/launch.py) — touched
# by the interrupt trap so a phase that has not started cannot start during the
# kill. Cleared at the next launch, so an interrupted run leaves one behind.
.campaign-stop

# okf-rag artifacts. `okf/` is a generated concept bundle — its authority is the
# pgvector store okf-rag maintains, and it is rebuilt from the archived findings
# by records/evidence/2026-08-26-claim-verification/build_okf.py. Committing it
# would put generated prose in the tree and give a stale copy equal standing
# with the store. `.okfrag/` is the staleness flag okf-rag writes on `status`.
okf/
.okfrag/

